 { IM Eric Rosen found himself in this position in an online game as Black. Can you find the strong move that he played here? } 1... { -KEY- } c5 $1 { Black has the semi-open e-file to work on, but for now White is keeping the e3 pawn well defended. This move will turn the e-file into an open file after ...cxd4, allowing Black to funnel his pieces into the White position. } 2. g5 $4 { In the game, White quickly went wrong. } ( 2. Rgf3 { was a more stubborn try, but after } cxd4 3. exd4 Qb4 $17 { Black's pressure in the centre is tough to deal with. } ) 
cxd4 $1 { Correct! White's situation was immediately critical after the powerful ...c5 break, but now the entire pawn chain is collapsing. } 3. f5 dxe3 $1 4. Nxe3 Nxg5 $19 { Black was up two pawns and went on to win the game. } 
