 { Black appears to be in serious trouble due to White's control over the c-file. However, they have one surprising move that holds the balance. Can you find it? } 1... { -KEY- } Rc8 $1 2. h4 ( 2. Rxc8 $4 Rxc8 { would land White in serious trouble, since a move like } 3. Rf1 { would lead to } Rc3 { with a deadly invasion along the open file. The alternative of } 3. Rxc8 $4 { is even worse, since after } Qa1 31. Bf1 Bh3 $1 { there is no way to stop a quick mate on f1. } ) 
Rxc2 { Correct! By eliminating one set of rooks Black takes away the strength of White's control over the c-file. Here's how play could continue: } 3. Rxc2 Qa1+ $1 { Not the only way to play, but I like this active approach. } 4. Kh2 Qd1 5. Qc7 Bg6 $11 { White still controls the c-file, but Black has plenty of counterplay of their own. } 
